pirical findings or performance differences observed between MinED and EM on BBH?", "evidence": "Inspected workspace environment and confirmed task.json specifies a design-only task without required compute or empirical execution. No local datasets or model codebases are pre-installed in /workspace.", "assumptions": ["The BBH benchmark consists of the standard 23 challenging subtasks from Suzgun et al. (2022).", "The alignment criteria operate at the post-generation answer extraction/evaluation stage, mapping model output text to canonical answers/options.", "Greedy decoding (temperature 0) is standard for BBH benchmarking to guarantee determinism."], "uncertainties": ["Specific formulation and candidate target set for MinED across free-form vs multiple-choice BBH tasks.", "Exact LLM model checkpoints and prompt structures tested in the source paper (ICLR 2024 #18013).", "Whether MinED is applied solely during evaluation scoring or also during in-context demonstration selection / scoring."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call_34419__thought__", "tool_call": {"id": "call_34419__thought__", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Proposed experimental design plan comparing MinED vs EM on BBH.\", \"uncertainties\": [\"Specific formulation and candidate target set for MinED across free-form vs multiple-choice BBH tasks.\", \"Exact LLM model checkpoints and prompt structures tested in the source paper (ICLR 2024 #18013).\", \"Whether MinED is applied solely during evaluation scoring or also during in-context demonstration selection / scoring.\"], \"answer\": \"### Proposed Experimental Design Approach\\n\\n#### 1. Research Question & Objective\\nThe core objective is to design an experimental study evaluating whether the proposed **MinED (Minimum Edit Distance)** alignment criterion outperforms the baseline **EM (Exact Matching)** alignment criterion on the **Big-Bench 